{"id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:linear-semilinear-quasilinear-fully-nonlinear","title":"def:linear-semilinear-quasilinear-fully-nonlinear","path":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.md","line":19,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.tex#def:linear-semilinear-quasilinear-fully-nonlinear","uses":["[[references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:kth-order-pde]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.tex","label":"def:linear-semilinear-quasilinear-fully-nonlinear","line":33,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Linear, Semilinear, Quasilinear, and Fully Nonlinear PDE]\n\\label{def:linear-semilinear-quasilinear-fully-nonlinear}\n\n\\uses{def:kth-order-pde}\n\n\\dcref{ch1:1.1-def-2}\n\\group{PDE Basics}\n\n\n\nFor (1):\n\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item The equation is \\emph{linear} if\n$$\\sum_{|\\alpha| \\leq k} a_\\alpha(x) D^\\alpha u = f(x)$$\nfor given $a_\\alpha$ and $f$; it is \\emph{homogeneous} when $f \\equiv 0$.\n\n\\item It is \\emph{semilinear} if\n$$\\sum_{|\\alpha|=k} a_\\alpha(x) D^\\alpha u + a_0(D^{k-1}u, \\ldots, Du, u, x) = 0.$$\n\n\\item It is \\emph{quasilinear} if\n$$\\sum_{|\\alpha|=k} a_\\alpha(D^{k-1}u, \\ldots, Du, u, x) D^\\alpha u + a_0(D^{k-1}u, \\ldots, Du, u, x) = 0.$$\n\n\\item It is \\emph{fully nonlinear} if its dependence on the highest-order derivatives is nonlinear.\n\\end{enumerate}\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Linear, Semilinear, Quasilinear, and Fully Nonlinear PDE] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a6c696e6561722d73656d696c696e6561722d71756173696c696e6561722d66756c6c792d6e6f6e6c696e656172\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FEvans%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter1%23def%3Akth-order-pde\">↗ def:kth-order-pde</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch1:1.1-def-2</span></span>\\group PDE Basics <p></p>For (1): <p></p><ol><li><p>The equation is <em>linear</em> if </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[ \\sum _{|\\alpha | \\leq k} a_\\alpha (x) D^\\alpha u = f(x) \\]\">\\[ \\sum _{|\\alpha | \\leq k} a_\\alpha (x) D^\\alpha u = f(x) \\]</span></p><p> for given <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$a_\\alpha $\">$a_\\alpha $</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span>; it is <em>homogeneous</em> when <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f \\equiv 0$\">$f \\equiv 0$</span>. </p></li><li><p>It is <em>semilinear</em> if </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[ \\sum _{|\\alpha |=k} a_\\alpha (x) D^\\alpha u + a_0(D^{k-1}u, \\ldots , Du, u, x) = 0. \\]\">\\[ \\sum _{|\\alpha |=k} a_\\alpha (x) D^\\alpha u + a_0(D^{k-1}u, \\ldots , Du, u, x) = 0. \\]</span></p></li><li><p>It is <em>quasilinear</em> if </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[ \\sum _{|\\alpha |=k} a_\\alpha (D^{k-1}u, \\ldots , Du, u, x) D^\\alpha u + a_0(D^{k-1}u, \\ldots , Du, u, x) = 0. \\]\">\\[ \\sum _{|\\alpha |=k} a_\\alpha (D^{k-1}u, \\ldots , Du, u, x) D^\\alpha u + a_0(D^{k-1}u, \\ldots , Du, u, x) = 0. \\]</span></p></li><li><p>It is <em>fully nonlinear</em> if its dependence on the highest-order derivatives is nonlinear. </p></li></ol> ","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: group"]},"previous":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:kth-order-pde","next":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:kth-order-system-pde","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:kth-order-pde","title":"def:kth-order-pde","label":"def:kth-order-pde"}],"